 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "digits is a string of 0-9 with the keypad 1 -> ABC, 2 -> DEF, 3 -> GHI, 4 -> JKL, 5 -> MNO, 6 -> PQR, 7 -> ST, 8 -> UVW, 9 -> XY, 0 -> Z. Each maximal run of one digit is split into consecutive groups, each of size 1 up to the number of letters of that digit; a group of size g produces the g-th letter. Return every distinct string obtainable this way, in ascending lexicographic order. An empty digits string returns an empty list.",
